<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yaruba dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1624–<a href="/years/1742">1742</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Ya'rubid dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yaruba dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> from 1624 to 1742. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasir-ibn-murshid">Nasir ibn Murshid</a> and his successors it united the country under Ibadi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imams</a>, drove the Portuguese from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muscat">Muscat</a> in 1650 and built a sea power that took Mombasa and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> towns on the East African coast. A civil war over the succession and a Persian invasion ended its rule, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-bu-said-dynasty">Busaidi dynasty</a> replaced it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yaruba-dynasty.jpg" alt="Yaruba dynasty" width="320" height="174" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Atsuya1 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ya%27ariba_Dynasty%27s_ensign.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
